# Vercel serves what it receives. Next.js only serves files under public/, so the
# artefacts at the repository root are not reachable — but they are excluded anyway,
# because "not reachable today" is a property of the framework rather than a decision,
# and the cost of being wrong here is customer contract prices on the open web.

# The operational dumps: sales transactions, receivables ageing, contract prices.
dumps/

# The pipeline, its docs, the approved masters (zmat, the RM tracker model, contract
# prices) and the session memory. None of it is needed to render a page.
.claude/
.agents/

# The old static dashboard and its data. data.json is the entire 6.5 MB payload every
# account used to download, and access.json holds the sign-in hashes it was guarded by.
# Both are superseded; neither should ever be served again.
data.json
access.json
index.html

# Local tooling.
tools/
supabase/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
docs/
